Rules:
  [C1] Use `std::unique_ptr` and `std::shared_ptr`.
  [C2] Use `std::optional` for nullable values.
  [C3] Use `std::variant` for sum types.
  [C4] Use concepts for template constraints.
  [C5] Use ranges for algorithms.
  [C6] Use `std::span` for view types.
  [C7] Use coroutines for async (C++20).
  [C8] Use modules instead of headers (C++20).

Pros:
  - Zero-cost abstractions
  - Maximum control
  - Modern features

Cons:
  - Template complexity
  - Compile times
  - Tooling

Alternatives:
  - Rust (safer)
  - Go (simpler)
  - Zig (modern)

